---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---
<SiteLayout title="Usage terms | PlaneDrawer" description="What PlaneDrawer is for, the limits of its sketches and how to keep your work safe.">
  <article class="document-page frame">
    <p class="eyebrow caption-3">Usage terms</p>
    <h1 class="heading-1">A sketch, not a construction plan.</h1>
    <p class="body-3">These notes describe the intended use and limitations of the sketchpad.</p>
    <section><h2 class="heading-5">For thinking about familiar spaces</h2><p class="body-3">PlaneDrawer helps you draw a first draft of rooms, walls and familiar details. It is not a substitute for a measured survey, professional plans, engineering or building advice.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="heading-5">Check before relying on a drawing</h2><p class="body-3">A sketch reflects what you enter. Verify dimensions and real conditions before making decisions about a space. Measurements in the editor use meters along wall centerlines.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="heading-5">Keep your own backup</h2><p class="body-3">Browser storage is not permanent. Export JSON copies of work you want to keep. SVG export produces a drawing for viewing or printing and cannot restore an editable plan.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="heading-5">Keep sensitive details out of shared files</h2><p class="body-3">Review labels and the layout before sharing an export. The app does not send the file for you or control how a recipient uses it.</p></section>
    <a href={base} class="button button-md">Back to PlaneDrawer</a>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
